        "original_id": "e312a912-a62c-5274-828b-5eb6afab9f8c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Florentius, Julian, Julius Caesar\n- Roles: praetorian prefect, Caesar, consul, emperor, perpetual dictator\n- Places: Roman Empire\n- Concepts: Roman Republic, civil wars, political conflict, assassination\n\nFacts:\n- In 44 BC, Julius Caesar was appointed perpetual dictator of the Roman Republic and was then assassinated.\n- The 500-year-old Roman Republic that preceded the Roman Empire was severely destabilized by a series of civil wars and political conflict.\n- The Roman Empire was known in Latin as \"Imperium Rōmānum\" and in Koine and Medieval Greek as \"Βασιλεία τῶν Ῥωμαίων.\"\n- Florentius was a Roman praetorian prefect under the Caesar Julian.\n- Florentius later became a consul.\n- Florentius fell from grace when Julian became emperor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
